{
  "dom_id": "question-166771",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "A meter of drill fabric costs $$3.48.$ If Anna bought one meter of cotton fabric and one meter of drill fabric, in total, she paid $$$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        .",
  "worked_solution": "In part 2, we found that one meter of cotton fabric costs $$3.95.$\n\nTo find the total cost, we need to calculate the value of $3.95+3.48.$\n\nFirst, we line up the decimal points:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,3\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,.\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,9\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,+\\,\\,\\,\\, &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,3\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,.\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,8\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,.\\,\\,\\,\\, &  & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we proceed by adding the two numbers just as we would with whole numbers:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\begin{aligned} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\, &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\begin{aligned} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,3\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,.\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,9\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,+\\,\\,\\,\\, &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,3\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,.\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,8\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,7\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,.\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,3\\,\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n3.95+3.48=7.43.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the total cost is $$7.43.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
